          %h2#Terminology Note on terminology
          %p
            Whitehead complained about the term
            %em cocone
            back in the old days, because of the seeming (though false) double dualization, so he used
            = succeed "." do
              %em mapping path space
          %p
            Somebody – maybe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"} Samuel Eilenberg
            – (– check –) suggested to Whitehead to use
            %em ne
            insteaad of
            %em cocone
            , jokingly cancelling one
            %em co
            against the other, as if both expressed abstract
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} duality
          %p
            Postnikov uses the term
            %em mapping cocylinder
            , while for on Whitehead’s complaint he comments:
          %blockquote
            %p we do not see a particular criminal in the cocone terminology, but will anyway not use it.
